<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karakorum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karakorum was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, established under Ögedei. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a> was subordinate to the Great Khan in Karakorum during Chagatai's lifetime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karakorum.jpg" alt="Karakorum" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erdene_Zuu_Monastery_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
